{
 "help": "usage: wgsextract lineage y-haplogroup [-h] [--download | --no-download] [--build {hg19,hg38,t2t}]\n                                       [--tree TREE] [--ancient] [--tree-links] [--help-all]\n\noptions:\n  -h, --help            show this help message and exit\n  --download, --no-download\n                        Allow missing public reference/model downloads; no sample files or\n                        genotypes are uploaded. Hosts and request data: docs/privacy.md. Default:\n                        config allow_reference_downloads, else off.\n  --build {hg19,hg38,t2t}\n                        Override the detected reference build for this run.\n  --tree TREE           Haplogroup tree: yfull (the pinned YFull YTree release), yfull_v10 (YFull\n                        10.01), ftdna, isogg, or a config.toml [y_trees.<id>] tree (default:\n                        config y_tree, else yfull).\n  --ancient             Use ancient-DNA marker tables.\n  --tree-links          Print YFull and FTDNA tree links.\n  --help-all            Show this help with the advanced options too, and exit.\n\nglobal options:\n  -i/--input, -o/--outdir, --genome, --ref, -t/--threads, -m/--memory, --json, --quiet, --debug,\n  --config and the other global options are accepted before or after the command; 'wgsextract\n  --help' lists them all.\n\n9 advanced options not shown; 'wgsextract lineage y-haplogroup --help-all' lists them.\n\nexamples:\n  wgsextract lineage y-haplogroup --input sample.cram\n\noutputs (in the output directory unless noted):\n  yleaf/: hg_prediction.hg, the per-sample .out/.fmf/.info reports and\n  run.json; prints the haplogroup and the tree's name and version.\n\nneeds:\n  bcftools, samtools; minutes on a 30x genome.\n",
